{
  "name": "14_seq_wraparound",
  "description": "a retransmission whose sequence number has wrapped past 2^32",
  "derivation": "p1 seq=100 len=100 sets the high-water mark to 200. p2 seq=4294967200 len=50 ends at 4294967250. Under 32-bit MODULAR comparison that is 246 sequence numbers BEFORE 200, so it is already-transmitted space -> RETRANSMISSION. A naive unsigned comparison (4294967250 <= 200?) would be False and would miss it, which is exactly what this fixture guards against. retrans = 1 of 2 seq-bearing, 50 retransmitted bytes.",
